[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
What the Next.js web application (`frontend/`) does as seen by its user and at its interfaces to the HTTP API, the
browser storage and AirBrief, written from the code as built. Every page (`frontend/app/**`) and component group
(`frontend/components/**`) is covered here. Low-level requirements exist in this issue only for `frontend/lib/`,
`components/three/flightPathGeometry.ts`, `components/shared/DeltaBadge.tsx`, `components/shared/UnitsToggle.tsx`
and `i18n/request.ts` (`llr-web.sdoc`, decision D-10); behaviour that lives only in pages and components is
verified at this level and says so in its verification note (open item OI-012). Design: `06-design/lld-web.md`. Interface: `03-system/icd/icd-web-ui.md`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Upload

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Choosing a log file
STATEMENT: >>>
The home page (`/`) shall take one flight log by drag and drop or through a file chooser labelled "Flight log file".
It shall pass on only a file whose name ends (case ignored) in `.ulg`, `.ulog`, `.bin`, `.log`, `.tlog`, `.bbl`,
`.bfl`, `.txt`, `.dat`, `.gz` or `.zip` and whose size is at most the limit in MB set by
`NEXT_PUBLIC_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB` (50 when unset or not a number). For more than one file, another ending or a larger
file it shall upload nothing and shall show which rule was broken ("Drop one log at a time.", "<name> is not a
flight log this server reads.", "<name> is larger than <mb> MB.").
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Verified at HLR level for now (D-10, OI-012); `app/page.tsx` and `components/upload/DropZone.tsx` have no LLR. The
Playwright smoke test gives an accepted `.ulg` to the file chooser. No test gives a rejected file; the three
rejection messages are checked by reading `DropZone.tsx` and `handleFile` in `app/page.tsx`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
