[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Upload request, options and errors
STATEMENT: >>>
The home page shall send the chosen file to the API as one multipart `POST /analyse` with the field `file`, plus
`airframe_label` when the user typed a label (trimmed; the input takes at most 40 characters),
`contribute_to_dataset=true` only when the user ticked "Contribute this log anonymously" (not ticked by default),
and `planning_brief_sha256` in lower case when the user entered a planning brief hash. A hash that is not exactly 64
hexadecimal characters shall stop the upload with a message. A token stored in the browser for that label shall be
sent in the header `X-Airframe-Token`. While the upload runs the page shall show the percentage sent and a cancel
button; cancelling returns to the idle form with no error. On status 200 or 202 the page shall add the report to
the browser's recent list and go to `/report/<report_id>`. On failure it shall show the API's `detail` text when
there is one and otherwise: for 401 or 403 that the airframe belongs to someone else or needs its token, with a
link to the airframe page; for 413 that the file is too large; for 429 that the upload limit is reached; for 503
(always, whatever the API sent) that the server is busy; for any other status "Server error (<status>)."; for no
connection "Network error. Is the API running?"; and after 10 minutes without an answer "Upload timed out.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The Playwright smoke test uploads a real log and follows the redirect to the report. The options and every error
branch are not exercised by a test; they are checked by reading `uploadLog` (LLR-WEB-006, LLR-WEB-007) and
`app/page.tsx`.
<<<
