[[SECTION]]
TITLE: The report page

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Progress and fetching the report
STATEMENT: >>>
For `/report/<id>` the Next server shall ask the API once for `GET /report/<id>` (not cached, 8 s limit). On 200
it shall render the report in the page it serves; on 404 it shall show "Report expired"; on 422 it shall show
"Analysis failed" with the API's reason. In every other case the browser shall poll `GET /status/<id>`, first after
1 s, then at intervals growing by a factor of 1.5 up to 5 s, and shall show a progress bar, the API's progress
message (or "Waiting for a free worker" while progress is 0) and the remaining time when the API gives one. When
the status is `complete` it shall fetch `GET /report/<id>` and show the report; a 202 answer there keeps it
polling. Polling shall end with: "Report expired" on 404; "Analysis failed" when the status is `failed` or a call
answers 422 or 500 (a reason starting with "interrupted" is replaced by a restart message); "Can't reach the
server" with a retry button after five failed calls in a row; "Still not finished" with a retry button after 10
minutes. Report pages shall carry `robots: noindex, nofollow`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The polling states are tested through `pollReport` (LLR-WEB-015, LLR-WEB-016) and the smoke test waits through
the progress view to the report. The server-side fetch (LLR-WEB-014) and the wording of each end state are checked
by reading `app/report/[id]/page.tsx`, `ReportLive.tsx` and `Problem.tsx`. The poller asks for the status at once
and waits 1 s only after the first answer (LLR-WEB-015 comment).
<<<
ALLOCATION: web
