[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Report header and score
STATEMENT: >>>
The report page shall show, first: the file name; the flight start (local time and UTC, or "Flight date not in
log"); vehicle type, airframe name and firmware where present; duration; file size; the overall score in a ring
with "/ 100" and the report's score label; the letter grade; the count of critical and of warning findings, each
linking to the findings; "No critical or warning findings" when the report is assessed and has neither; the
executive summary text as the report holds it; "Assessed <n> of <total> checks."; when `assessed_fraction` is
below 1 the share of the weighted score that was assessed, as a percentage; and, when `parse_warnings` is not
empty, the number of parser warnings as a link to the flight details. It shall offer "Print" and "Copy link"
(copies the page address). The executive summary carries no mark of whether the optional AI rewrote it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Verified at HLR level in this issue; `ReportHeader.tsx` and `ScoreCircle.tsx` have no LLR yet. The smoke test
checks that the header shows the uploaded file's name. The other items are checked by reading the two components.
<<<
