[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Not assessed is shown as not assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
On the report page a report whose `assessed_fraction` is 0, whose grade is `-` or whose label contains "not
assessed" shall be shown with a grey ring with no arc, a dash in place of the score, the words "Not assessed", no
grade badge, no "No critical or warning findings" badge and the sentence that none of the checks could run. A
module with `skipped` true or `assessed` false shall be listed under the module scores as "Not assessed" with its
reason, in muted text, with no bar and no number. The page description for link previews shall say "Not assessed"
in place of a score. On the airframe page a module score that is null or missing shall be a gap in the trend line
and "not assessed" as the latest value; in the comparison table it shall read "not assessed"; in the recent list a
grade of `-` shall read "Not assessed" with no colour.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test renders a not-assessed report or module. A review reads `isAssessed` and `isReportAssessed`
(LLR-WEB-038), `ScoreCircle.tsx`, `ReportHeader.tsx`, `ModulePerformanceChart.tsx`, `RecentReports.tsx`,
`app/airframe/[label]/page.tsx` and `app/compare/page.tsx`. The places that still show the raw overall score of a
not-assessed flight are listed in `lld-web.md` section 6.
