[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Findings list and timeline
STATEMENT: >>>
The report page shall list the findings under "Findings (<count>)", most severe first (critical, warning, info,
good). Critical and warning findings shall be shown directly, critical ones opened; info and good findings shall
sit behind a button "<n> other checks (info and passed)". Findings in one category whose titles share the text
before `: ` or ` - ` (written with a long dash) shall be shown as one card with a row per finding and the worst
severity. Each finding shall show its severity as an icon and a word, its category icon, title, the recommendation,
the plain-English explanation, the technical summary, its parameter changes, its confidence as a percentage with
the level when given, and its time window in the log as `t m:ss` to `m:ss` when it has one. Buttons shall filter
by severity. A timeline from 0:00 to the end of the log shall carry one marker per timed finding, the armed
windows as grey bands, and a click on a marker shall open and scroll to that finding. With no findings the section
shall read "No findings. Every check that could run on this log passed."; with none critical or warning, "No
critical or warning findings.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The smoke test checks that the findings section is shown for a real report. Grouping is tested at LLR level
(LLR-WEB-041, LLR-WEB-042). Sorting,
filtering, the timeline and the two empty texts are checked by reading `FindingsList.tsx`, `FindingCard.tsx`,
`GroupedFindingCard.tsx`, `FindingParts.tsx` and `FindingsTimeline.tsx`; none of these components has an LLR yet.
<<<
