[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parameter sheet, copy and download
STATEMENT: >>>
When `param_change_sheet` is not empty the report page shall show it as a table: parameter name, current value,
suggested value (each followed by the unit when the report gives one) and the reason text as the report holds it.
It shall offer the whole sheet as text in the Mission Planner format (`NAME,VALUE` lines) or the QGroundControl
format (tab-separated rows with a type column), by "Copy all" and by a download named `flightmd_changes.param`
or `flightmd_changes.params`, and each row as one line by its own copy button. The copy and the download always
hold every entry of the sheet. The format first offered shall be QGroundControl when the report looks like PX4 and
Mission Planner otherwise, and the page shall say which autopilot it picked for. Values shall be written without
exponent notation. The page shows no extra mark on, and asks no confirmation for, an entry whose reason says that
another check disagrees.
<<<
