STATEMENT: >>>
Under "Flight details" the report page shall show the module scores (worst first, each with a bar, an icon and
"<n> / 100"); flight start in UTC; duration; arm count; maximum altitude, maximum speed and distance in the chosen
units; vehicle; airframe name; firmware; hardware; flight modes; place name; the day's weather (description,
maximum wind, temperature range) when present; the log format by name; the log SHA-256 (shortened, copied whole);
processing time; schema version; and the time the report was generated. A missing value shall show as a long dash.
When `parse_warnings` is not empty the section shall hold a closed disclosure "<n> parser warnings: parts of the
log that were skipped or repaired" that lists each distinct warning once when opened.
