[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Report search and optional AI answers
STATEMENT: >>>
The report page shall offer a search over the report that runs in the browser and makes no request: a question
about parameters lists the change sheet; a question naming a check gives that module's score, finding count and
key metrics, or "not assessed" with the reason; any other text lists the findings and sheet entries containing it.
With the "Use AI" switch on, a question (at most 500 characters) shall be sent as `POST /ask/<report_id>` with a
60 s limit, and the answer shall be shown under the label "AI answer, from this report only" with the note that
the answer is to be checked against the findings. When the API answers that no provider is configured the switch
shall be disabled for the rest of the visit and the question answered by the search. A 429 shall show "Too many
questions for now. Try again in a minute."; another failure the API's text or "The AI request failed
(<status>).". AI answers are never written into the findings, the score or the sheet shown on the page.
<<<
