[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Recent reports kept in the browser
STATEMENT: >>>
The home page shall list the reports this browser uploaded, newest first, at most 20, from the browser's own
storage and from no server call: file name linking to the report, flight or upload date, vehicle, grade and score
once the report has been opened, the airframe label linking to its page, and "probably expired" for an untagged
report older than one hour. The user shall be able to remove one entry, clear the list, tick two entries and open
their comparison with the earlier flight as `a`, and, for an entry uploaded with the contribute option, withdraw
the contribution (`DELETE /dataset/<contribution_id>`; a 404 counts as done; another failure shows the API's text
or "Could not withdraw the contribution (<status>)."). A report opened from a shared link is not added.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The API has no listing of uploads (SYS-029), so the only way back to a report is its address; the browser keeps
the addresses of its own uploads.
<<<
