[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Comparison of two flights
STATEMENT: >>>
`/compare?a=<id>&b=<id>` shall call `GET /diff?a=<a>&b=<b>` and `GET /report/<id>` for both. When both reports
give a flight start and `a` is the later one the page shall reload with the two swapped. It shall show a card per
flight (file name, score, label, grade, flight date, vehicle) linking to its report, the change in overall score,
a table of module scores for both with the change, a table of key metrics for both with the change in the chosen
units and without colour, the findings resolved, the findings new, and the categories still present with their
severity in each flight. A score change smaller than 0.5 shall read "no change"; a rise "+n better" in green with
an up arrow; a fall "-n worse" in amber with a down arrow. When the two reports differ in autopilot or vehicle
type the page shall warn that the scores are not directly comparable. Without both ids it shall say that two are
needed; a 404 from the diff shall read "One or both reports were not found or have expired."; another failure the
API's text or "Cannot compare these two flights (<status>).".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The score-change badge is tested at LLR level (LLR-WEB-061). No test renders `app/compare/page.tsx` or
`FindingDiff.tsx`, which have no LLR yet; they are checked by reading, with `getDiff` (LLR-WEB-010).
<<<
