[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe page: trends and history
STATEMENT: >>>
`/airframe/<label>` shall call `GET /trends/<label>`, `GET /airframe/<label>/config` and `GET
/airframe/<label>/changes`, each with the stored token. It shall show the number of tagged flights; the overall
score per flight as a line from 0 to 100; one line chart per module score; one line chart per key metric in the
chosen units; each chart with a table of its values; and the flight history, newest first, with file name linking
to the report, upload time, grade and score, and a tick box. Ticking two flights shall offer their comparison with
the older one as `a`. With no flights it shall say so and link to the upload page. When trends or config fail for
a reason other than access the page shall show the API's text or "Could not load the trend history (<status>)." /
"Could not load the airframe settings (<status>)." with a retry button; when only the changes call fails the
applied-changes section is left out. A label that cannot be decoded shall read "This airframe link is malformed.".
<<<
