[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe access token
STATEMENT: >>>
The web application shall keep each airframe token it receives (in the answer to an upload or to any airframe
call) in the browser's local storage under the lower-cased label, shall send it only in the request header
`X-Airframe-Token`, and shall never put it in an address. When an airframe call answers 401 or 403 the airframe
page shall show, in place of its content: for an airframe nobody has claimed, an explanation and a "Claim this
airframe" button that sends an empty `PUT /airframe/<label>/config` and keeps the token returned; otherwise a
password field to paste the token, titled "That access token doesn't match" when the answer was 403 or a token was
already stored, with a button to forget the stored one. With a token stored the page shall show it masked, with
buttons to reveal it, copy it and forget it.
<<<
