[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Display rules for every page

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unit preference
STATEMENT: >>>
Every page shall carry a unit selector with metric (m, m/s, degrees C), imperial (ft, mph, degrees F) and aviation
(ft, kt, degrees C). The choice shall be kept in the browser and applied on every page of that browser. Altitude,
distance, speed and temperature values, and key metrics that are altitudes, shall be converted when drawn and
shown with the unit of the chosen system. Conversion shall happen only in the value put on the screen: the report
object, the browser's stored data, the parameter values, the parameter file, the applied-change records sent to
the API and the exports hold the report's own values. The server render and the first browser render are metric.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The selector, the stored choice and every conversion are tested. That no converted value is written back is
checked by reading every caller of `useUnits`, `toUnit`, `fmtQty` and `Labels.convert`: each passes the result
straight to the render.
<<<
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-037

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Light and dark theme
STATEMENT: >>>
Every page shall offer a switch between a dark and a light theme. The choice shall be kept in the browser; with
no choice kept the theme follows the browser's `prefers-color-scheme`, dark when that is not light. The theme
shall be set before the first paint. The theme changes colours only; severity is always given by an icon and a
word as well as a colour.
<<<
