[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Links to AirBrief
STATEMENT: >>>
When `NEXT_PUBLIC_AIRBRIEF_URL` is set at build time: a report with a GPS path shall offer "Audit airspace in
AirBrief", opening `<airbrief>/w/view?m=flight-audit&report_url=<this report's address, URL-encoded>` in a new
tab; and a report that carries a `planning_brief_sha256` of 64 hexadecimal characters shall offer "Open in
AirBrief", opening `<airbrief>/w/report?brief=<hash in lower case>`. The planning brief hash shall be shown
(shortened, copied whole) whether or not AirBrief is configured. Without the setting neither link is shown.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
SYS-024 asks only that the planning brief hash be carried in the report. The two links are added so the flight
can be opened in the planning tool; no system requirement asks for the audit link.
<<<
