[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Error text and containment
STATEMENT: >>>
For a failed API call the page shall show the API's own `detail` text when the answer carries one (the first
message of a validation error list), and otherwise its own text for that call with the HTTP status; a call that
gets no answer in 20 s (60 s for downloads and AI questions) shall read "The server took too long to answer." and
one that cannot connect "Network error. Is the API running?". A part of the report that fails while drawing
(a chart, the charts section, the map, the 3D view) shall be replaced by "<part> unavailable: the data in this
report could not be drawn." and the rest of the page shall stay; if the report as a whole cannot be drawn the page
shall say so and point to the exports. An error outside these shall show "Something broke on this page" with a
retry button. An unknown address shall show "Page not found".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The error object and the timeout and network mapping are covered at LLR level (LLR-WEB-002, LLR-WEB-003,
LLR-WEB-018). No test renders `ErrorBoundary.tsx`, `app/error.tsx` or `app/not-found.tsx`; they are
checked by reading.
<<<
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-036
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Numbers, times and missing values
STATEMENT: >>>
Numbers shall be shown with thousands separators and a fixed maximum of decimals for their kind; a value that is
missing or not a finite number shall be shown as a long dash, never as 0. Scores shall be shown as "<n> / 100",
rounded to a whole number. Positions in the log shall be shown as `m:ss` or `h:mm:ss` from the start of the log.
Flight start and report times shall be shown in UTC marked "UTC", and in the header also in the viewer's local
time with its zone. Only a text starting with a full ISO date and `T` is taken as a date. Parameter values shall
be shown and written with at most 7 significant digits and no exponent.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: web
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-037
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-036

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-026
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Limits of use shown with the report
STATEMENT: >>>
The report page and its printed form shall state that the report is advisory, that a clean report is not a release
to service, and that parameter changes need review and a test flight before use; the parameter sheet shall mark an
entry whose reason says another check disagrees before it can be copied or downloaded.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Not built: `messages/en.json` holds no such statement and the home page tells the user the report gives "the exact
parameter changes to make".
<<<
