  VALUE: SYS-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Configuration, language and response headers
STATEMENT: >>>
The browser code shall call the API at `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (fixed at build time; when unset, the page's own
origin on an https page and `http://localhost:8000` otherwise). The Next server shall call it at `API_URL`, then
`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, then `http://localhost:8000`. All user-facing text shall come from `messages/en.json`; the
one locale is `en` and no address carries a locale. Every response of the web application shall carry
`X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and `Referrer-Policy:
strict-origin-when-cross-origin`. The page header shall link to the API documentation at
`<NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL>/docs` when that variable is set.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement states how the web application finds the API or which headers it sends; the design needs
both.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test checks the environment fallbacks or the headers. A review reads `lib/api.ts` (LLR-WEB-001),
`lib/serverApi.ts` (LLR-WEB-014), `i18n/request.ts` (LLR-WEB-062), `next.config.js` and `app/layout.tsx`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: web
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-036

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-WEB-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Colours from the shared design tokens
STATEMENT: >>>
The colours of both themes shall come from `frontend/design/tokens.json`, turned into `frontend/app/tokens.css`
by `frontend/scripts/tokens-to-css.mjs` before `dev` and `build`; the generated file is committed and shall match
the JSON. In both themes body text shall reach a contrast of 4.5:1, critical text 7:1 and caution, advisory and ok
text 4.5:1 on each of the three background colours.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for a contrast level or a shared token file; the file is shared with AirBrief so the
two tools look alike, and the contrast limits keep severity text readable in both themes.
<<<
